1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.149 line:2 align:center
The Epic Sepsis Model ships
with a widely used health record

2
00:00:05.149 --> 00:00:07.059 line:2 align:center
and runs at hundreds of US hospitals.

3
00:00:07.059 --> 00:00:11.985 line:2 align:center
It scores every adult
inpatient every 15 minutes

4
00:00:11.985 --> 00:00:15.573 line:2 align:center
and alerts when that
score crosses a threshold.

5
00:00:15.573 --> 00:00:22.283 line:2 align:center
Its vendor reported an
AUC between 0.76 and 0.83.

6
00:00:22.483 --> 00:00:26.816 line:2 align:center
Wong and colleagues validated
it at Michigan Medicine:

7
00:00:26.816 --> 00:00:34.706 line:2 align:center
27,697 patients and
38,455 hospitalizations,

8
00:00:34.706 --> 00:00:40.283 line:2 align:center
of which 2,552, or 7%, had sepsis.

9
00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:42.822 line:2 align:center
The AUC was 0.63,

10
00:00:42.822 --> 00:00:48.492 line:2 align:center
with a 95% interval from 0.62 to 0.64.

11
00:00:48.492 --> 00:00:55.320 line:2 align:center
The authors also report
per-horizon AUCs of 0.72 to 0.76,

12
00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.501 line:2 align:center
then explain why those are misleading:

13
00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:02.483 line:2 align:center
the predictions are not
independent of each other.

14
00:01:02.683 --> 00:01:07.756 line:2 align:center
At the vendor's threshold
of 6, sensitivity was 33%,

15
00:01:07.756 --> 00:01:10.635 line:2 align:center
so two thirds of sepsis
cases were never flagged.

16
00:01:10.635 --> 00:01:14.556 line:2 align:center
The positive predictive value was 12%.

17
00:01:14.556 --> 00:01:18.592 line:2 align:center
Alerts fired on 18% of
all hospitalizations:

18
00:01:18.592 --> 00:01:23.283 line:2 align:center
8 patients to evaluate
for every sepsis case.

19
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:28.564 line:2 align:center
Now ask what the alert added.
Of the 2,552 sepsis cases,

20
00:01:28.564 --> 00:01:31.164 line:2 align:center
843 were flagged,

21
00:01:31.164 --> 00:01:36.231 line:2 align:center
and of those only 183 had not
already received timely antibiotics.

22
00:01:36.231 --> 00:01:44.017 line:2 align:center
Of the 1,709 that were missed,
1,030 were treated in time anyway.

23
00:01:44.217 --> 00:01:48.027 line:2 align:center
Two lessons. Validate
locally before deployment,

24
00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:51.823 line:2 align:center
because a vendor's AUC came
from a vendor's population,

25
00:01:51.823 --> 00:01:56.068 line:2 align:center
not yours. And measure the
increment over current practice,

26
00:01:56.068 --> 00:01:57.616 line:2 align:center
not the model on its own.

27
00:01:57.616 --> 00:02:03.880 line:2 align:center
A model is worth deploying only if
it changes what happens to a patient.
